{
 "format": "cpn-document",
 "version": 1,
 "name": "MM1",
 "declarations": "(* An M/M/1 queue: customers arrive at random (on average every 100 time units) and are\n   served one at a time (on average 50 time units). Known answers: the server is busy half the\n   time, on average 1 customer is in the system, and a customer spends 100 time units in it. *)\ncolset UNIT = unit timed;\ncolset CUST = int timed; (* a customer: the time it arrived *)\nvar c : CUST;\nval lambda = 0.01; (* arrivals per time unit *)\nval mu = 0.02;     (* services per time unit *)\nfun delay rate = round (exponential rate);\n",
 "pages": [
